course: dictionary
lesson: 11211
title: Wonderfully and how words tell us more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell us how something happens. «Wonderfully» is an adverb, and it does exactly that. It means in a very good, pleasing or delightful way.
explain: «That was wonderfully done,» says the Woman. The clues are the praise and the word done: the job was done very well, and it pleased her. Check by swapping in well: «That was well done» still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Wonderfully can also mean very or extremely, in a good way. In «wonderfully warm», it means very warm, and warm is a nice thing to be. Look at the words near it to tell which meaning fits.
fact: Wonderfully is an adverb: it tells you how something is done, or how much.
fact: «Wonderfully» means in a very good, pleasing or delightful way.
fact: «Wonderfully» can also mean very or extremely, in a good way, as in «wonderfully warm».
fact: Toad talks «so wonderfully about the trip» that the others end up agreeing with him: wonderfully tells us how he talks.
fact: Adverbs like «wonderfully» often end in -ly, but not every word ending in -ly is an adverb.
exercise: «That was wonderfully done,» says the Woman. What does wonderfully mean here? | *In a very good, pleasing way | In a slow, sleepy way | In a loud, angry way
exercise: In «wonderfully warm», what does wonderfully mean? | Only just | Not at all | Cold and wet | *Very, in a good way
exercise: «Toad talks wonderfully about the trip.» Which word tells us how Toad talks? | *wonderfully | about | talks | trip
test: «The garden smelled wonderfully of roses.» What does wonderfully mean here? | Not at all | In a rough, harsh way | *In a very pleasant way | In a slow, tired way
test: Nadia says «wonderfully» is just another word for «well». Which swap shows the meaning is close? | «She was wonderfully kind» becomes «She was quietly kind» | «She was wonderfully kind» becomes «She was sadly kind» | «She was wonderfully kind» becomes «She was extremely kind» | *Both are close, but «extremely» fits the meaning of very in a good way best
exam: In «She was wonderfully kind», which word could replace wonderfully without changing the meaning? | quietly | *extremely | sadly | barely
